     I have lost many a game to those annoying floating eyes.  I never
intend to attack them, but I get lots of scenarios like:
Walking along at a pace where I can see what I'm running into before I hit
it, the game suddenly pulls a disk read and an extra left move gets put
into the buffer.  "You miss.  You are frozen by the floating eye's gaze!"
Enter a little dog stage left.  Exit game.
---
Have a wand of make invisible.  Zap "C", game pulls an overlay read.  By
the time I see "Nothing happens" I've already hit the down arrow, and
that game goes out the window as well.

     I NEVER INTEND TO HIT THOSE GUYS!  But my score list is half-full of
good beginnings that ended from accidentally (usually unpreventably)
hitting one of those @#$%ing things.
     Something like:
"The eye looks at you penetratingly.  Really attack? [yn]"
would be *real* nice.  In addition, if you can't see the eye at any point,
the gaze should be broken.  I'm not quite sure whether that's still the
case, but in previous versions the thing can die and BE EATEN and you're
still frozen by its gaze.  Rediculous!
     On the same note, I've lost several plusses off of weapons via green
molds and acid blobs I also never intended to hit.  Something like:
"That acid looks awfully corrosive.  Really attack? [yn]"
would help prevent such mishaps.  This would, naturally, only occur
if you were using a weapon on it, while the floating eye message
would occur on any attack.
     Also, if that particular eye or blob had been attacked before, ideally
you'd stop getting that (at this point annoying) message, since obviously
you're in the fighting mood.  That's not incredibly important, though.
(The only case I can think of is if one was trying to kill a green mold with
a rustproof weapon [or an acid blob].  Then that could get annoying.)

     Nymphs: It doesn't seem practical that a nymph can just walk right up
and talk anything you have, then disappear.  *Some* men are that stupid, but
a Valkrie?  Dunno if I've had a V charmed by a nymph, but they still rob
her blind.
     I don't have any particular solution- I'd quote "Keep a tight leash
on that wench" (physically, a]pply a leash and she wouldn't be able to
teleport away) but that gets a bit kinky... especially in a realm equipped
with blindfolds, ropes and bullwhips...

